# Angular Frontend

- Use standalone components; do not introduce NgModules unless required by a library.
- Prefer `inject()` for DI in new code.
- Use Signals for local UI state; use `computed`/`linkedSignal` when derived state is needed.
- Prefer Signal Forms on Angular 21+ when adding new forms.
- Feature folders own routes, pages, components, services, and models for that feature.
- Put HTTP clients and feature state close to the feature that owns them.
- `core/` is for app-wide singletons only (auth, interceptors, config).
- `shared/` only for reuse across 2+ features; no feature-specific code.
- Keep templates lean; move non-trivial logic into component class or services.
- Scaffold and file layout follow `.cursor/rules/angular-project.mdc` (`ng generate`, one folder per page/layout component, `templateUrl` for pages, `--skip-tests` by default).
- After meaningful frontend changes, run `ng build` (and tests when touching behavior).
